What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/iobuf_pool_premap_stats
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-block@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		[RO] Reports whether allocations from a block I/O buffer pool
		obtained a persistent DMA-IOMMU mapping.  The file contains one
		``name=value`` counter per line, or ``disabled`` when the queue
		has no buffer pool.

		``attempts`` counts syntactically valid allocation commands which
		reached the current pool, including commands which later fail folio
		allocation, DMA mapping, or io_uring registration.  ``successes``
		counts commands which both retained a DMA-IOMMU mapping and completed
		io_uring registration.  ``fallbacks`` counts successful registrations
		without a retained map, including providers with no DMA device and
		best-effort mapping failures.  Failed commands therefore need not
		appear in either ``successes`` or ``fallbacks``.

		The remaining counters describe DMA premap failures: no translating
		IOMMU, unsupported page size, IOVA space exhaustion, IOVA
		misalignment, other allocation failures, link failures, and final
		IOTLB synchronization failures.  ``strict_rejections`` overlaps the
		applicable failure category and counts strict page-size requests which
		were rejected instead of falling back to dynamic DMA mapping.  Folio
		checkout and io_uring registration errors are not categorized here.

		Counters are monotonic for the lifetime of the attached pool and reset
		when that pool is replaced.  Each line is sampled independently, so a
		read concurrent with registrations is not a transactional snapshot.
